## Template 1 — Parent Issue: `problem-record.yml`

```yaml
name: Problem Record Tracker
description: >
  Create a parent tracking Issue for a Problem Record (PR) managed in ServiceNow.
  Preventive Tasks derived from this PR will be created as sub-issues linked to
  this parent.
title: "[PR] <PRB number> — <short description>"
labels:
  - "PR:New"
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        ---
        # 🔍 Problem Record Tracker
        ---
        This Issue is the **parent tracking record** for a Problem Record (PR)
        managed in **ServiceNow**.
        > ℹ **Do not record the full Problem Record here.**
        > This Issue exists to group and track all **Preventive Tasks** derived
        > from the PR within the sovereign GitHub boundary.
        > Each Preventive Task will be created as a **sub-issue** linked to
        > this parent.

  - type: input
    id: pr-number
    attributes:
      label: "* Problem Record Number (ServiceNow)"
      description: The ServiceNow Problem Record number this tracker is linked to.
      placeholder: "PRB0110337"
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: input
    id: component
    attributes:
      label: Component
      description: The affected component as recorded in ServiceNow.
      placeholder: "GCID-NW-010"
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: input
    id: service-offering
    attributes:
      label: Service Offering
      description: The affected service offering as recorded in ServiceNow.
      placeholder: "GCID-Network-WAN-Edge"
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: dropdown
    id: priority
    attributes:
      label: "* Priority"
      description: Priority as set in ServiceNow.
      options:
        - 1 - Very High
        - 2 - High
        - 3 - Moderate
        - 4 - Low
        - 5 - Planning
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: dropdown
    id: data-processing-security
    attributes:
      label: Data Processing & Security
      options:
        - NONE
        - Personal Data
        - Sensitive Personal Data
        - Confidential
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: input
    id: due-date
    attributes:
      label: "* Due Date"
      description: >
        Overall due date for all Preventive Tasks under this PR (YYYY-MM-DD).
      placeholder: "YYYY-MM-DD"
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: pr-summary
    attributes:
      label: "* Problem Summary"
      description: >
        Brief summary of the Problem Record — what happened and why
        Preventive Tasks are required.
      placeholder: |
        - Problem description:
        - Root cause (if identified):
        - Why Preventive Tasks are required:
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: preventive-tasks-overview
    attributes:
      label: Preventive Tasks Overview
      description: >
        List all Preventive Tasks to be created as sub-issues. One row per task.
        Update the Sub-issue # column once each sub-issue has been created.
      placeholder: |
        | # | Subject | Assigned Team | Due Date | Sub-issue # |
        |---|---------|---------------|----------|-------------|
        | 1 |         |               |          |             |
        | 2 |         |               |          |             |
        | 3 |         |               |          |             |
        | 4 |         |               |          |             |
        | 5 |         |               |          |             |
    validations:
      required: false

  - type: checkboxes
    id: pr-checklist
    attributes:
      label: Pre-submission Checklist
      options:
        - label: The ServiceNow Problem Record number has been referenced above.
          required: true
        - label: A summary of the problem and reason for Preventive Tasks has been provided.
          required: true
        - label: This Issue contains no Customer or Confidential Data.
          required: true

  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        ---
        ### Next Steps
        1. After submitting this parent Issue, populate the **Project side-panel**
           fields: LoB, Priority, Due Date.
        2. Create **one sub-issue per Preventive Task** using the
           `Preventive Task` Issue template.
        3. Link each sub-issue back to this parent using the
           **Parent Issue** Project field.
        4. Track overall progress via the **All Problem Records** Project view.
        > ⚠ Sub-issues may be assigned to **different teams**.
        > Each team works their own sub-issue independently.
        ---
```

